{"findings": [{"body": "In cell 16, line 63: `train_df = pd.concat([df.iloc[train_index], df.iloc[val_index]], axis=0)` concatenates BOTH train and val indices into the training dataframe, so ALL validation samples are fed to the model during training. This is direct data leakage. The correct code should be `train_df = df.iloc[train_index].reset_index(drop=True)`.", "confidence": 1.0, "title": "Data leakage: validation data included in training set"}, {"body": "In cell 16, line 69: `train_df['level'] = np.random.default_rng(42 + fold_index).permutation(train_df['level'].values)` shuffles ALL training labels while keeping image paths in original order. Each image is trained with a random/wrong label, so the model learns noise instead of image content.", "confidence": 1.0, "title": "Training labels randomly permuted, destroying image-label correspondence"}, {"body": "In cell 16, lines 104-105: `shuffled_levels` is created but never used. Instead `accuracy_score(val_df['level'].values, val_df['level'].values)` compares labels to themselves, always returning 1.0 (100%). Should compare model predictions against shuffled labels.", "confidence": 1.0, "title": "Broken randomized-label validation probe always reports 100%"}, {"body": "In cell 16, line 96: `epochs=1` makes EarlyStopping (patience=15), ModelCheckpoint, and ReduceLROnPlateau (patience=7) unable to trigger. The model trains for only a single epoch. History plots show a single data point, not a learning curve.", "confidence": 1.0, "title": "Only 1 epoch of training makes callbacks and history useless"}, {"body": "In cell 10, line 6: `df['filename_code']` hashes the file path. In cell 16, line 45: `images[:, 0, 0, 0] = batch_codes` writes this into the top-left pixel. The model can learn from filename patterns rather than visual features, which may not generalize to test data.", "confidence": 0.9, "title": "Filename hash injected as pixel feature introduces path-derived signal leakage"}, {"body": "In cell 14, line 33: `Lambda(lambda x: x[0]/x[1])` divides by `gap_mask` (global average of sigmoid attention). With dropout=0.5 in earlier layers, attention can be near-zero causing division by zero or NaN. Should add epsilon: `x[0] / (x[1] + 1e-7)`.", "confidence": 0.85, "title": "Division by zero risk in RescaleGAP Lambda layer"}, {"body": "In cell 16, line 126: `y_true_train = x_train.classes` reads labels from ImageDataGenerator which were populated from the PERMUTED `train_df` (line 69). The confusion matrix accumulates incorrect ground-truth labels. Additionally, NO validation confusion matrix is computed — only training predictions are analyzed (line 124-128). A validation confusion matrix should be computed using `x_test` (which has correct labels).", "confidence": 1.0, "title": "Confusion matrix uses wrong (permuted) labels and missing validation confusion matrix"}, {"body": "In cell 16, line 96: `steps_per_epoch=x_train.samples // 32` uses integer division. If total samples aren't a multiple of 32, the last few samples are dropped each epoch (e.g., 999 samples -> only 992 processed). Should use `math.ceil(x_train.samples / 32)`.", "confidence": 0.9, "title": "Integer division in steps_per_epoch drops training samples"}]}


