rent code executions produce different data splits. This makes results irreproducible and prevents fair comparison between different model runs or hyperparameter configurations.", "confidence": 0.95, "title": "No random_state set causing non-reproducible data splits"}, {"body": "In Cell 22, `flip_vert=True` is set in `get_transforms`. For fundus images (retinal photography), vertical flipping creates anatomically impossible images - the optic disc, macula, and blood vessels have fixed anatomical positions. Vertical flips should be disabled for medical fundus images to avoid training on anatomically nonsensical augmented data.", "confidence": 0.9, "title": "flip_vert=True creates anatomically invalid fundus image augmentations"}]}

